#
# Conformance case: occurrent/causal-transitive
# AC: YAMATO occurrent mereology (#1081) — causalPartOf transitivity.
#
# ex:A causalPartOf ex:B, ex:B causalPartOf ex:C. The transitivity rule must
# derive causalPartOf(A, C); the causal⊑temporal lift then yields temporalPartOf
# for each pair. The chase seeds only from input.nq; this is the mirror axiom.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/occurrent/causal-transitive/> .

ex:A logic:causalPartOf ex:B .
ex:B logic:causalPartOf ex:C .
